16 0 obj
<< /A 63 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing the role of an Agentic AI Agent in agriculture. Four main areas are highlighted: Crop Monitoring and Health Management, Soil and Nutrient Management, Irrigation and Water Management, and Pest and Disease Control. Each area lists related tasks, such as real-time plant disease detection and smart irrigation scheduling, demonstrating how AI aids in optimizing agricultural processes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 64 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing an agricultural system interacting with different layers. The environment includes elements like tractors and plants. The system consists of a Perception Layer, Cognitive Layer, and Actuation Layer, linked to a Knowledge Base and Communication Layer, indicating data flow and processing.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 65 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating a two-layer architecture. The Perception Layer includes Sensors, Data Acquisition Module, Pre-processing Unit, Feature Extraction Module, and Environment Context Handler. The Cognitive Layer comprises Reasoning Engine, Decision-Making Module, Learning Module, Knowledge Base Handler, and Communication Handler. Arrows indicate the flow of information from the Perception Layer to the Cognitive Layer.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the interaction between the Cognitive Layer and Actuation Layer. The Cognitive Layer includes modules: Reasoning Engine, Decision-Making Module, Learning Module, Knowledge Base Handler, and Communication Handler. The Actuation Layer comprises Execution Controller, Actuator Interface Module, Task Scheduler, Feedback Module, and Communication Handler. Arrows depict information flow between layers.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Smart farming system diagram showing interconnected components: fields of crops and livestock, sensors, tractors, a satellite, and control center. Agents for irrigation, nutrients, pests, decision coordination, weather, and crop health are managed. Farmers and machinery receive alerts for optimized operations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Six images show tomato leaves affected by late blight. Each leaf has dark brown lesions and wilting, indicating disease progression. Variably sized patches are visible across the leaves.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 69 0 R /Alt (Two rows of three images each show plants labeled as either \215crop\216 or \215weed.\216 The top row features a crop on the left and weeds in the center and right. The bottom row displays a weed on the left, a crop in the center, and a weed on the right. Soil is visible in all images.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 50 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 70 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a machine learning model architecture. The top section illustrates a shared backbone with convolution and max pooling layers followed by dense blocks. The mid-section splits into two pathways: a classification head with layers for pooling, connection, activation, and loss evaluation, and a detection head with a feature pyramid network, convolutional layer, prediction heads, and post-processing layer. Local model weights feed into FedAvg, building a global model that connects to classification and object detection outputs.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 51 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 71 0 R /Alt (Two graphs show loss curves for machine learning models over 50 epochs. \(a\) MobileNetV2: Training and validation losses decrease, stabilizing around 0.1. \(b\) DenseNet-121: Similar trend with both losses stabilizing slightly below 0.1.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 52 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 72 0 R /Alt (Panel \(a\) shows accuracy curves for MobileNetV2 over 50 epochs, with both training and validation accuracy increasing and stabilizing around 0.95. Panel \(b\) displays DenseNet121's accuracy curves, reaching similar stability with both training and validation accuracy near 0.98.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 53 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 73 0 R /Alt (Two graphs show model performance over epochs. The left graph displays training and validation loss, both decreasing significantly. The right graph shows training and validation accuracy, both increasing and converging. The graphs illustrate the model's learning progress.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 53 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 74 0 R /Alt (Six line graphs showing training and validation losses over 100 epochs. Top row: train/box_loss, train/cls_loss, train/dfl_loss; all decrease from around 1.2 to 0.2. Bottom row: val/box_loss, val/cls_loss, val/dfl_loss; follow similar downward trends.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 54 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /A 75 0 R /Alt (Six line charts showing the loss progression over 100 epochs. The top row displays training losses for box, class, and DFL, each decreasing from about 1.2 to 0.2. The bottom row shows validation losses for the same categories, also decreasing similarly.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 54 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
29 0 obj
<< /A 76 0 R /Alt (Two confusion matrices compare the performance of MobileNetV2 and DenseNet121 models on classifying plant diseases. Both matrices indicate predicted labels versus true labels, with darker green representing higher values. MobileNetV2 and DenseNet121 show high accuracy for classifying diseases like Late Blight and Healthy conditions, with a color scale indicating quantities up to 383.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 55 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
30 0 obj
<< /A 77 0 R /Alt (Four separate images of soil with green plants and weeds enclosed in boxes labeled as \215crop\216 and \215weed.\216 The images depict small patches of soil with varied plant growth identified for analysis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 57 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
31 0 obj
<< /A 78 0 R /Alt (Plants in soil with green bounding boxes and percentages indicating crop and weed identification. Various plants are labeled, such as crops at 72% and weeds at 68% accuracy, among others.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 58 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
32 0 obj
<< /A 79 0 R /Alt (Confusion matrix for a global model depicting classification accuracy for various plant diseases and healthy conditions. Labels include Late Blight, Septoria Leaf Spot, Bacterial Spot, Leaf Mold, and more. Cells indicate the number of true versus predicted labels, with values ranging from zero to three hundred and eighty-nine. The color gradient from light to dark green represents increasing counts.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 58 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
33 0 obj
<< /A 80 0 R /Alt (Login and dashboard screens of the Agri-Connect app for smart farming. The login screen has fields for username and password. The dashboard shows field monitoring data like temperature, humidity, and soil moisture, with forecasts and irrigation controls. The design features agricultural imagery.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 59 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
